# Backend Architecture Standards

## Separation of Concerns
- Thin Controllers / Routes: Route handlers must only validate request schemas, call Services, and return responses.
- Service Layer: All domain logic, calculations, business invariants, and transactional logic live in Service classes.
- Database Access: Use repository or query builder abstractions. Optimize query paths and indexes.
- Clean Architecture / Hexagonal: Isolate domain core from infrastructure adapters.
- Reference Skills: Consult `./.agent/skills/clean-code/SKILL.md` and `./.agent/skills/api-patterns/SKILL.md`.
